  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Cefuroxime is a second-generation cephalosporin antibiotic used to treat a range of bacterial infections, including pneumonia, sinusitis, pharyngitis, urinary tract infections, gonorrhea, Lyme disease, and skin infections. It is an approved antibiotic that is widely used in human medicine, available both alone and in combination with other antibacterials.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q413728&quot;>Wikidata Q413728</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>cefuroxime</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J01DC02, S01AA27</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01112&quot;>DB01112</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5479529&quot;>5479529</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:3515&quot;>3515</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q413728&quot;>Q413728</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C16H16N4O8S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>424.384 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
